    "created_at": "2025-04-28T18:10:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-04-28T18:10:12Z",
    "body": "@domenic's comment there:\n\n> I indeed editorially prefer the current approach, as adding attribute changed steps to sync a boolean is more cumbersome. I'll mark this and the previous comment as off-topic though since it's unrelated to the issue discussed here.\n\nIf it's useful to make the case, I worry the existing spec will diverge from many implementations which will want to implement this as a member boolean rather than a function pointer which returns a boolean, and so each implementation will have to introduce - by trial and error - the necessary attribute changed steps to sync the boolean.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
